{"seconds": 60.6, "exit": 0, "final": "OK. So **Bc5** is a powerful quiet move that sets up the Rd8 tactic and threatens a7. This appears to be the key move.\n\n---\n\n**Best move: Bc5**\n\n**Main line:** Bc5 Bxa6 (or Rf8) Rd8+ Kxd8 (forced, or king moves) and White wins material (the a7 pawn is undefended, the rook on h8 is attacked).\n\n**Motif:** Deflection / Attraction (moving the bishop from d6 to c5 deflects Black's pieces and sets up Rd8, which attacks both king and rook)\n\n**Coaching Note (80 words):**\nYour d6 bishop was active but needed to work with your rook. Bc5 does three jobs: it attacks the a7 pawn, supports a rook invasion on d8, and prepares a double attack. When Black grabs the a6 pawn or moves the rook to defend, Rd8+ comes with check\u2014now the rook on h8 is trapped. Look for quiet moves that set up a \"fork with check\" rather than moving into immediate tactics.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bc5\", \"line\": [\"Bc5\", \"Bxa6\", \"Rd8+\", \"Kxd8\", \"Bxa7\", \"Rh7\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27", "move": "Rd8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27", "move": "Bxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27", "move": "Bf4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27", "move": "Bf3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2k4r/p5pp/P2Bp3/1b2Pp2/2p1p3/8/4B1Pb/3R1K2 w - - 0 27", "move": "Rc1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args"